\\ge 1$). $\\tau(a_i) \\ge \\tau(2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 13^{i-1}) = 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot i = 4i \\ge 4$. The condition holds.\nThis gives the second family of solutions: integers $N = 2^k \\cdot 3^j \\cdot m$, where $k \\ge 3$ is an odd integer, $j$ is an integer satisfying $j \\ge (k+1)/2$, and $m$ is a positive integer whose prime factors are all at least 7."
